questions=[
 ('1','Who owns A, and does the signed trust actually hold title?','— unverified','Read deed, trust schedule and amendments with the trustee.', 'Changes authority to transfer or sell.','ownership'),
 ('1','What type of trust, what powers and which beneficiaries?','— unverified','Obtain signed trust and amendments privately; ask counsel about distribution powers.', 'Affects allocation, timing, tax and contest risk.','notice'),
 ('1','Does A qualify for an income-tax basis adjustment?','— unverified','Ask a tax lawyer to assess title, estate inclusion and trust facts.', 'An unadjusted basis can change the sale analysis materially.','trustbasis'),
 ('1','Was A the transferor’s principal residence and can an eligible recipient occupy it on time?','— unverified','Document residence and relationship; ask the county assessor about special circumstances.', 'Determines eligibility for family-home reassessment relief.','prop19'),
 ('1','What is the complete gross estate, prior taxable gifts, debts and available spousal exclusion?','— unverified','Prepare a confidential estate inventory with advisers; include all relevant interests.', 'Determines filing and estate tax; no actual headroom can be calculated yet.','estate'),
 ('1','What is the property’s date-of-death fair market value?','— unverified','Obtain a qualified appraisal at the relevant date; retain private documentation.', 'Sets the usual basis and affects reassessment and sale proceeds.','basis'),
 ('1','Are there co-beneficiaries, equalization duties, debts or liens?','— unverified','Review trust, loans, liens and distribution terms privately.', 'Could constrain the ability or timing to keep or sell.','notice'),
 ('1','What are the actual assessed values and parcel-specific tax rates?','— unverified','Read county bill and tax-rate-area details for each property.', 'A simple percentage misses direct charges and reassessment timing.','prop13'),
 ('1','What are the dwelling replacement costs and actual insurance quotes?','— unverified','Get owner-occupied and rental/owner-occupied-multiunit quotes as applicable.', 'Premium, deductible, exclusions and vacancy terms alter cash flow and risk.','cdi'),
 ('1','How much are lawful market rent, vacancy and management costs for A?','— unverified','Get independent current comparables and professional management estimates.', 'Rental economics and legal limitations can change the ranking.','hud'),
 ('1','What are the current leases and rent-control status for B?','— unverified','Review leases, building history and Rent Board rules privately.', 'Income and lawful increases cannot be inferred from a benchmark.','sfRent'),
 ('2','Who pays utilities and what are actual bills?','— unverified','Review a year of bills, meter counts, provider and lease terms.', 'Water, sewer and electricity are not fixed by the ZIP code.','water'),
 ('2','What solar tariff and interconnection date apply?','— unverified','Review interconnection agreement and annual true-up privately.', 'Future export credits and fixed charges may differ.','solar'),
 ('2','What repairs and capital improvements are likely?','— unverified','Obtain inspections, multi-year invoices and contractor estimates.', 'Maintenance, capital basis and one-off risks affect both costs and tax.','rental'),
 ('2','What is land versus building value if A is rented?','— unverified','Use a defensible appraisal and tax preparer’s depreciation schedule.', 'Depreciation and later recapture can materially change the comparison.','rental'),
 ('2','What are the income, brackets and potential passive-loss limits?','— unverified','Prepare confidential taxpayer-specific scenarios with a CPA.', 'Flat scenario rates are not the actual combined tax.','rental'),
 ('2','What is the type and beneficiary treatment of inherited cash or retirement accounts?','— unverified','Inventory account types and designations privately with an adviser.', 'IRA distributions and cash or securities have different tax treatment.','ira'),
 ('2','What is the desired living arrangement and the value of housing services?','— preference not established','Compare nonfinancial needs, work, accessibility and alternate housing privately.', 'A financial ranking omits the benefit of living in a home.','invest'),
 ('2','How would sale proceeds be invested, and how much liquidity is needed?','— preference not established','Set an investment policy, risk tolerance and deposit-insurance plan.', 'Returns, tax drag and sequence risk are assumptions, not guarantees.','fdic'),
 ('3','What laws, valuation and insurance conditions will apply at the event?','— not knowable yet','Recheck official sources regularly and immediately before a decision.', 'Future law and prices can make today’s model obsolete.','cbo'),
]
